About the Company

Aras is a leading provider of digital thread solutions for product lifecycle management (PLM) and engineering AI. As one of the fastest growing PLM companies, our AI-native, low-code platform enables the rapid delivery of flexible solutions that connect teams across disciplines and functions to critical product data and agentic AI throughout the product lifecycle and extended value chain. The world's largest manufacturers leverage Aras Innovator to manage complex product lifecycles, accelerate innovation, improve operational efficiency, and bring products to market faster. We collaborate with companies in some of the world's most innovative industries, including automotive, industrial equipment, aerospace and defense, high tech, and life sciences.

Who We Are And What We Do Aras Innovator is a dynamic product that has a flexible system of customization in accordance with specific needs and specific requirements, and this versatility is one of the reasons why our software is so successful around the world. Today, Aras suite is used by companies such as Microsoft, Airbus, Boeing, General Motors, Kawasaki, Motorola, Honda, Freudenberg, Imperial Tobacco Group, Schaeffler, ECCO, Carestream Health, GETRAG and other Fortune members.

About the Role

We are looking for an experienced .Net Fullstack Developer to join our team that works on Aras Innovator – an industrial low-code platform for creating rich enterprise applications.

Qualifications

Higher technical education;

Required Skills

10+ years of experience in commercial projects;
C # knowledge, experience in .NET;
OOP, SOLID principles understanding;
Experience with MS SQL Server and good command of T-SQL;
Experience with React;
Good knowledge of web technologies (HTML, JavaScript/TypeScript);
Knowledge of design patterns;
Strong knowledge of Agile;
Understanding of the HTTP protocol, REST, and OData;
Possession of Git (or other DVCS);
Upper-intermediate (reading/writing/speaking) levels;
Strong team player with excellent collaboration and communication skills, committed to continuous improvement of team processes
Ability to quickly switch between different contexts.
Must be eligible to work in Poland

Preferred Skills

Knowledge of TDD, experience in creating Integration tests;
Experience in business correspondence;
MongoDB
Knowledge of Azure or AWS.

Must be eligible to work in Poland

